- Instruct patients to report any signs of facial swelling, difficulty breathing, or swelling of the lips/tongue immediately, as this could indicate angioedema.
- Warn patients about the potential for peripheral edema (swelling of the ankles or feet) and to report it if it becomes bothersome.
- Female patients of childbearing potential should be counseled on the risks of fetal harm and instructed to stop the medication and notify their doctor immediately if they become pregnant.', '("Aliskiren"[Mesh] OR "Aliskiren"[tiab]) AND ("Amlodipine"[Mesh] OR "Amlodipine"[tiab])');

