**Clinical Considerations:** It is not expected to cause fetal harm and can be used during pregnancy if clinically indicated.', 'Due to negligible systemic absorption, it is considered safe for use during lactation.', '{"trimester_1": "Safe", "trimester_2": "Safe", "trimester_3": "Safe"}', 'This combination provides essential metabolic substrates to the crystalline lens to maintain ATP production, thereby preventing or slowing down lens opacification.', '["Cytochrome C acts as an electron carrier in the mitochondrial respiratory chain, aiding in oxidative phosphorylation.", "Sodium succinate serves as an intermediate metabolite in the Krebs cycle, promoting the production of ATP.", "Adenosine provides the structural purine base required for the synthesis of ATP, supplying energy for the vital functions of the lens.", "Nicotinamide acts as a precursor for NAD/NADP, essential coenzymes involved in cellular redox reactions and ATP creation.", "Together, these components support the metabolic integrity and transparency of the crystalline lens."]', '**Moderate:**
- **Other Ophthalmic Drops:** Concurrent use may wash out the medication. *Management:* Wait at least 15 minutes between the instillation of this product and any other ophthalmic solutions.', '**Lens Opacification**
