**Infections:** Do not use in the presence of untreated bacterial, fungal, or viral skin infections. If concomitant skin infections are present, an appropriate antimicrobial agent must be used.', '- Relief of the inflammatory and pruritic manifestations of corticosteroid-responsive dermatoses (e.g., eczema, psoriasis, contact dermatitis, lichen planus).', '**Hypersensitivity:** Contraindicated in patients with a history of hypersensitivity to betamethasone or any of the excipients.

**Skin Infections:** Contraindicated as monotherapy in primary bacterial, fungal, or viral (e.g., herpes simplex, varicella) infections of the skin.', '- Burning, stinging, and irritation at the application site
- Skin atrophy (thinning of the skin)
- Striae (stretch marks)
