- For Vitamin C overdose, maintain adequate hydration to promote excretion and prevent kidney stones.
- For Vitamin D toxicity (hypercalcemia), institute a low-calcium diet, administer intravenous fluids (normal saline) to promote diuresis, and consider loop diuretics (e.g., furosemide) to enhance calcium excretion. In severe cases, corticosteroids or bisphosphonates may be required to reduce serum calcium levels.', '- Store at room temperature below 30°C (86°F).
