**Clinical Considerations:** Maternal hyperglycemia can lead to fetal hyperinsulinemia and subsequent neonatal hypoglycemia. Monitor maternal and fetal glucose levels closely.', 'Use with caution during pregnancy, monitoring blood glucose to prevent maternal and fetal hyperglycemia. It is generally considered safe during lactation as it is a normal physiological substrate.', '{"trimester_1": "Safe", "trimester_2": "Safe", "trimester_3": "Safe"}', 'Dextrose 25% provides a highly concentrated source of calories and water, rapidly elevating blood glucose levels.', '["Intravenous dextrose is rapidly distributed and taken up by cells via glucose transporters.", "Inside the cell, it is metabolized via glycolysis and the citric acid cycle to produce ATP, providing a dense source of energy.", "This high caloric supply rapidly reverses severe hypoglycemia and minimizes the breakdown of body protein.", "When co-administered with insulin, it drives extracellular potassium into the intracellular space, effectively lowering serum potassium levels."]', '**Blood Products:** Do not administer simultaneously with blood through the same infusion set due to the risk of pseudoagglutination or hemolysis. 
*Management:* Flush lines with normal saline between infusions or use separate lines.
**Corticosteroids:** May exacerbate glucose intolerance and hyperglycemia. 
