  - *Children >14 years:* Use adult dosing (25-50 mg PO 2-3 times daily).
- *Note:* Safety and efficacy in children <2 years of age have not been established (except for IV use in neonates for PDA).', '[{"target_group": "Children 2-14 years (Inflammatory Disorders)", "min_age_months": 24, "max_age_months": 168, "dosing_type": "weight_based", "parameters": {"mg_per_kg_per_day_min": 1, "mg_per_kg_per_day_max": 4, "divided_doses_per_day": [2, 3, 4], "absolute_max_daily_dose_mg": 200, "note": "Start at lower end of range. Administer with food or milk to minimize GI irritation."}}]', '- **Mild to Moderate Renal Impairment:** Caution should be exercised when giving indomethacin to patients with renal impairment. Monitor renal function closely.
- **Advanced Renal Disease (CrCl <30 mL/min):** Avoid use, as it may precipitate acute renal failure.', '- Administer orally immediately after meals, with food, or with milk to minimize gastrointestinal irritation.
