Data are not available regarding the presence of clascoterone or its metabolites in human milk, the effects on the breastfed infant, or the effects on milk production. Consider the developmental and health benefits of breastfeeding along with the mother''s clinical need for the drug.', '{"trimester_1": "Not established", "trimester_2": "Not established", "trimester_3": "Not established"}', 'Clascoterone is an androgen receptor inhibitor that competes with dihydrotestosterone (DHT) in the sebaceous glands, reducing sebum production and inflammation associated with acne.', '["Clascoterone penetrates the skin and enters the sebocytes and hair follicle cells.", "It acts as a competitive antagonist at the intracellular androgen receptors.", "By binding to these receptors, clascoterone prevents the binding of potent endogenous androgens, specifically dihydrotestosterone (DHT).", "This blockade inhibits androgen-induced gene transcription responsible for sebum production and the release of inflammatory cytokines.", "The reduction in sebum and inflammation alters the microenvironment, making it less favorable for the proliferation of Cutibacterium acnes, thereby improving acne vulgaris."]', '**Other Topical Acne Medications (e.g., Retinoids, Benzoyl Peroxide):**
