**Clinical Considerations:** Unlikely to cause fetal harm. Use during pregnancy only if clearly needed.', 'It is not known whether these ingredients are excreted in human milk. Because systemic absorption is minimal, it is generally considered safe for use during lactation. Use with caution.', '{"trimester_1": "Safe", "trimester_2": "Safe", "trimester_3": "Safe"}', 'This combination provides local anesthesia (benzocaine) along with counterirritant and cooling effects (camphor and menthol) to rapidly relieve mucosal pain.', '["Benzocaine is an ester-type local anesthetic that blocks voltage-gated sodium channels in nerve endings, preventing the generation and conduction of pain signals.", "Menthol stimulates cold-sensitive TRPM8 receptors in the skin and mucosa, producing a cooling sensation that distracts from pain and provides a soothing effect.", "Camphor acts as a mild counterirritant, stimulating nerve endings to produce a warming sensation that masks underlying pain.", "Together, they provide rapid, temporary relief of mucosal irritation and pain."]', '**Moderate:**
