**Clinical Considerations:** Use during pregnancy only if the potential benefit justifies the potential risk to the fetus. Avoid use on large areas, in large amounts, or for prolonged periods during pregnancy.', 'It is not known whether topical administration results in sufficient systemic absorption to produce detectable quantities in breast milk. Caution should be exercised. Do not apply to the breast area prior to nursing to avoid accidental ingestion by the infant.', '{"trimester_1": "Not established", "trimester_2": "Not established", "trimester_3": "Not established"}', 'This combination provides the potent anti-inflammatory action of betamethasone with the targeted antibacterial activity of fusidic acid against common skin pathogens.', '["Fusidic acid is a steroidal antibacterial agent that inhibits bacterial protein synthesis.", "It binds to elongation factor G (EF-G) on the bacterial ribosome, preventing its release and halting the translation process, effectively killing susceptible bacteria (primarily Staphylococcus aureus).", "Betamethasone valerate is a potent corticosteroid that binds to intracellular glucocorticoid receptors.", "This inhibits the release of inflammatory mediators (prostaglandins, leukotrienes), rapidly reducing the severe erythema, edema, and intense pruritus associated with the inflammatory dermatosis."]', '**Moderate:**
