**Renal and Hepatic Impairment:** Use with caution; increased risk of toxicity. Monitor renal and hepatic function prior to initiation and periodically during therapy.
**Pulmonary Toxicity:** Cases of severe pulmonary toxicity, including interstitial pneumonitis, pulmonary fibrosis, pulmonary edema, and adult respiratory distress syndrome (ARDS), have been reported. Discontinue if unexplained dyspnea or severe pulmonary toxicity develops.
**Infusion Time:** Prolonged infusion times (>60 minutes) and dosing more frequently than weekly have been shown to increase toxicity.
**Capillary Leak Syndrome:** Cases have been reported; discontinue if symptoms develop.
**Posterior Reversible Encephalopathy Syndrome (PRES):** Can occur; monitor for headache, lethargy, confusion, or visual changes.', '- **Non-Small Cell Lung Cancer (NSCLC):** First-line treatment of locally advanced (Stage IIIA or IIIB) or metastatic (Stage IV) NSCLC in combination with cisplatin, or as palliative monotherapy.
- **Pancreatic Cancer:** First-line treatment for locally advanced or metastatic adenocarcinoma of the pancreas, including patients refractory to 5-fluorouracil.
