**Infections:** Profound immunosuppression (especially decreased CD4+ T-cells) increases the risk of opportunistic infections (e.g., PCP, herpes zoster). Prophylactic therapy should be considered.
**Tumor Lysis Syndrome (TLS):** Increased risk in patients with a high tumor burden. Ensure adequate hydration and consider prophylactic allopurinol or rasburicase.
**Transfusion-Associated Graft-Versus-Host Disease (TA-GVHD):** Fatal TA-GVHD has been observed in patients receiving non-irradiated blood products. All blood products must be irradiated prior to transfusion.
**Handling:** Fludarabine is a cytotoxic agent. Avoid contact with skin and eyes; avoid inhalation. Follow safe handling and disposal procedures.', '- **B-Cell Chronic Lymphocytic Leukemia (CLL):** Treatment of adult patients with B-cell CLL who have not responded to or whose disease has progressed during treatment with at least one standard alkylating-agent containing regimen.', '**Severe Renal Impairment:** Contraindicated in patients with creatinine clearance (CrCl) <30 mL/min due to the risk of severe toxicity from drug accumulation.
**Decompensated Hemolytic Anemia:** Contraindicated due to the risk of exacerbating life-threatening autoimmune hemolytic anemia.
**Pregnancy and Lactation:** Contraindicated due to severe teratogenicity and potential for serious adverse reactions in nursing infants.
**Live Vaccines:** Concomitant use of live vaccines is contraindicated due to profound immunosuppression and the risk of fatal disseminated vaccine-derived infections.', '**>10%**
