- If repeat application is needed, dry the site again before reapplying.
- When using a spray device, strictly follow the manufacturer''s recommended pressure and distance guidelines to avoid air/gas embolism.', '**Intravascular Injection:** Accidental intravascular injection can cause life-threatening thromboembolic events, disseminated intravascular coagulation (DIC), and severe anaphylaxis.', '- If intravascular injection occurs, immediately stop the procedure.
- Provide aggressive supportive care, including cardiovascular and respiratory support.
- Manage thromboembolic complications or DIC according to standard critical care protocols.', '- Storage requirements vary by specific product formulation (e.g., some require freezing at ≤ -18°C, others require refrigeration at 2°C to 8°C).
