- **Severe (Ingestion):** Numbness of the mouth/throat, gastrointestinal upset, and theoretically, systemic local anesthetic toxicity (CNS excitation followed by depression, cardiovascular collapse) if massive amounts are ingested.', '- **Local Overdose:** Wash the affected area thoroughly with soap and water. Discontinue use.
- **Ingestion:** Provide supportive care. Do not induce vomiting due to the risk of aspiration and loss of gag reflex from oral anesthesia. Monitor vital signs and neurologic status.', '- Store at room temperature (20°C to 25°C).
- Keep the container tightly closed.', '- Use this medication exactly as directed. Do not use it more often or apply it to larger areas of your body than recommended.
