**Salicylism:** Salicylic acid can be absorbed systemically. Caution in patients with renal or hepatic impairment, as they are at higher risk for salicylate toxicity.

**Visual Disturbances:** Use of topical corticosteroids may be associated with systemic effects including cataracts and glaucoma. Avoid contact with eyes.', '- Treatment of hyperkeratotic and dry corticosteroid-responsive dermatoses, such as psoriasis (scalp and non-scalp), chronic atopic dermatitis, neurodermatitis, and seborrheic dermatitis.', '**Hypersensitivity:** Contraindicated in patients with a history of hypersensitivity to betamethasone, salicylic acid, or any component of the preparation.

