Iodine is excreted in human milk and can cause transient hypothyroidism in the nursing infant. Use with caution; avoid application to the breast area and avoid prolonged use.', '{"trimester_1": "Not established", "trimester_2": "Not established", "trimester_3": "Contraindicated"}', 'Povidone-iodine is a broad-spectrum microbicidal agent that releases free iodine, which oxidizes microbial cell constituents and inactivates proteins.', '["Povidone-iodine is a complex of the polymer povidone and iodine.", "Upon contact with the skin, the complex slowly releases free elemental iodine.", "Free iodine rapidly penetrates the cell walls of bacteria, viruses, fungi, and protozoa.", "It oxidizes key cellular constituents and iodinates proteins, leading to irreversible microbial cell death."]', '- **Lithium:** Concurrent use may result in additive hypothyroid effects. **Management:** Avoid concurrent use.
