It is unknown whether glycopyrronium is distributed in human breast milk. Because many drugs are excreted in human milk, caution should be exercised. Consider the developmental and health benefits of breastfeeding along with the mother''s clinical need.', '{"trimester_1": "Not established", "trimester_2": "Not established", "trimester_3": "Not established"}', 'A long-acting muscarinic antagonist (LAMA) that produces bronchodilation by competitively inhibiting acetylcholine at M3 receptors in airway smooth muscle.', '["Glycopyrronium is a specific, long-acting antimuscarinic agent (anticholinergic).", "Upon inhalation, it binds competitively to muscarinic receptors in the bronchial smooth muscle.", "It exhibits high affinity and slow dissociation from the M3 receptor subtype.", "By blocking the M3 receptors, it prevents acetylcholine-induced bronchoconstriction.", "This leads to prolonged relaxation of airway smooth muscle and sustained bronchodilation."]', '**Other Anticholinergic Agents:**
