- **Inflammatory Ear Conditions:** Management of inflammatory conditions of the external auditory meatus complicated by susceptible bacterial infections.', '- **Tympanic Membrane Perforation:** Contraindicated in patients with a known or suspected perforated eardrum due to the high risk of middle/inner ear ototoxicity.
- **Viral or Fungal Infections:** Contraindicated in primary viral (e.g., herpes simplex, varicella) or fungal infections of the ear, as corticosteroids can exacerbate these conditions.
- **Tuberculous Lesions:** Contraindicated in tuberculous infections of the ear.
- **Hypersensitivity:** Contraindicated in patients with a known allergy to lidocaine (or other amide local anesthetics), betamethasone, chloramphenicol, or any component of the formulation.', '- **Common:** Localized burning, itching, or stinging sensation upon instillation.
- **Less Common:** Localized erythema, rash, or contact dermatitis.
