There are no adequate and well-controlled studies of sofosbuvir and daclatasvir in pregnant women. Animal studies do not indicate direct or indirect harmful effects with respect to reproductive toxicity. However, if this regimen is administered with Ribavirin, the combination is strictly contraindicated in pregnancy due to Ribavirin''s known teratogenicity.

