Discontinue treatment if signs of hypersensitivity or angioedema (swelling of the face, lips, tongue, or eyelids) occur.', '- Symptomatic treatment of acute secretory diarrhea in adults, infants, and children, used as an adjunct to oral rehydration therapy when rehydration alone is insufficient to control symptoms', '**Hypersensitivity:** Contraindicated in patients with a known hypersensitivity to racecadotril or any of the excipients. Rationale: Risk of severe allergic reactions, including angioedema.
**Invasive Diarrhea:** Contraindicated in patients with bloody or purulent stools and fever. Rationale: Indicates invasive bacterial enteritis; reducing secretion without treating the infection may worsen the clinical outcome.
