3. **Supportive Care:** Monitor vital signs, ECG, and urine output continuously. Treat hypotension with fluids and vasopressors if necessary.', 'Store at 20°C to 25°C. Protect from light. Discard discolored solutions.', 'Take this medication in the morning to avoid waking up at night to urinate. Stand up slowly from a sitting or lying position to prevent dizziness or fainting. You may need to eat potassium-rich foods (like bananas or orange juice) or take a supplement; follow your doctor''s advice. Report any ringing in the ears, severe muscle cramps, or extreme weakness immediately.', '("Bumetanide"[Mesh] OR "Bumetanide"[tiab]) AND (Heart Failure[Mesh] OR Edema[Mesh] OR Diuretics[Mesh])');
- **Hyperphosphatemia in Chronic Kidney Disease:** Used off-label as a phosphate binder to reduce serum phosphate levels in patients with renal failure.', '- **Hypersensitivity:** Contraindicated in patients with a known hypersensitivity to aluminum salts or any component of the formulation.
