**MAOI Therapy:** Caution should be taken when administered with, or up to 21 days after administration of, monoamine oxidase inhibitors (MAOIs) due to the risk of exaggerated adrenergic effects (hypertensive crisis).', '- **Dilatation of the Pupil (Mydriasis):** For diagnostic procedures such as funduscopy, slit lamp examination, and retinal photography.
