**Osteonecrosis of the Jaw (ONJ):** Has been reported. Perform a routine oral exam prior to initiation and advise patients to maintain good oral hygiene.', '- **Osteoporosis:** Indicated for the treatment of osteoporosis in postmenopausal women at high risk for fracture (defined as a history of osteoporotic fracture or multiple risk factors for fracture), or patients who have failed or are intolerant to other available osteoporosis therapy.', '- **Hypocalcemia:** Contraindicated in patients with uncorrected hypocalcemia. Rationale: Romosozumab rapidly increases bone formation and mineralization, which can acutely drive calcium into the bone, exacerbating systemic hypocalcemia.
- **Systemic Hypersensitivity:** Contraindicated in patients with a history of systemic hypersensitivity (e.g., angioedema, erythema multiforme) to romosozumab or its excipients. Rationale: Risk of severe anaphylactic reactions.', '**>10%**
