Animal reproduction studies have not been conducted. It is not known whether it can cause fetal harm when administered to a pregnant woman. Anaphylactoid reactions in the mother can lead to fetal distress or death. Use during pregnancy only if clearly needed and the potential benefit outweighs the risk.

