- **Hysterosalpingography:** Contraindicated during the menstrual period or when menstrual flow is imminent; in the presence of pelvic infection; during pregnancy; or within 6 months after termination of pregnancy or 30 days after conization or curettage.', '- **Common:** Flushing, sensation of heat, pain at the injection site, nausea, vomiting, headache, dizziness, metallic taste.
