- Wash hands immediately after application unless the hands are the treated area.', '- **Topical Overexposure:** Exaggerated local adverse reactions such as severe erythema, stinging, blistering, and contact dermatitis.
- **Systemic Toxicity:** Extremely rare due to low percutaneous absorption.', '- **Topical Overexposure:** Discontinue application immediately. Wash the affected area gently with mild soap and water to remove residual medication. Apply a bland emollient or a mild topical corticosteroid if severe contact dermatitis develops.
- **Accidental Ingestion:** Provide symptomatic and supportive care. Gastric lavage may be considered if a large amount is ingested recently.', '- Store at room temperature between 15°C and 30°C (59°F and 86°F).
- Keep the tube tightly closed.
- Protect from excessive heat and freezing.', '- Instruct patients to complete the full course of treatment, even if symptoms improve within a few days, to prevent recurrence of the infection.
