- Discontinue use once the inflammation is controlled, and switch to an antifungal-only product if the fungal infection persists.', '- Chronic overapplication leads to severe local skin atrophy, striae, and telangiectasia.
- Systemic absorption can cause Cushing''s syndrome (moon face, weight gain), hyperglycemia, and HPA axis suppression.', '- **Supportive Care:** Discontinue the topical corticosteroid gradually by reducing the frequency of application to prevent rebound inflammation and adrenal insufficiency.', 'Store at controlled room temperature 20°C to 25°C (68°F to 77°F).', '- Apply only a very thin layer of the medicine to the affected areas. Using more will not make it work faster but will increase the risk of skin damage.
- Do not use this medicine for longer than 1 week for jock itch/ringworm, or 2 weeks for athlete''s foot, unless your doctor tells you to.
