- Protection of inflamed anorectal surfaces to help make bowel movements less painful', '**Hypersensitivity:** Contraindicated in patients with a known hypersensitivity to phenylephrine, pramoxine, or any of the inactive ingredients (glycerin, petrolatum), as it can cause severe contact dermatitis or anaphylaxis.', '- Localized allergic reactions (contact dermatitis)
- Mild, transient burning or stinging upon application
- Erythema or worsening of local irritation', 'C', '**Risk Summary:** There are no adequate and well-controlled studies in pregnant women. Systemic absorption of phenylephrine and pramoxine from topical rectal application is generally minimal. Use during pregnancy only if clearly needed.', '**Pregnancy:**
Category C. While systemic absorption is low, phenylephrine has vasoconstrictive properties. It should be used cautiously during pregnancy.

