It is unknown whether these components are distributed into breast milk following topical rectal administration. However, due to minimal systemic absorption, it is generally considered safe during lactation. Use with caution.', '{"trimester_1": "Safe", "trimester_2": "Safe", "trimester_3": "Safe"}', 'A combination preparation that reduces swelling, provides local anesthesia, and protects inflamed anorectal tissues.', '["Phenylephrine acts as a local alpha-1 adrenergic receptor agonist, causing vasoconstriction of the dilated blood vessels in the anorectal mucosa, thereby reducing tissue swelling.", "Pramoxine acts as a local anesthetic by reversibly blocking sodium channels in the sensory neuronal membranes, preventing the transmission of pain and itch signals.", "Glycerin acts as a hyperosmotic agent and humectant, drawing moisture to the area to soothe irritated tissues.", "Petrolatum forms a physical, occlusive barrier over the inflamed tissues, preventing moisture loss and reducing mechanical friction during bowel movements."]', '**Monoamine Oxidase Inhibitors (MAOIs):**
