  - Children >10 kg: 100 mg (2 mL).', '[{"target_group": "Infants and Children", "min_age_months": 4, "max_age_months": 216, "dosing_type": "weight_based", "parameters": {"mg_per_kg_per_day_min": 0, "mg_per_kg_per_day_max": 100, "divided_doses_per_day": [1], "absolute_max_daily_dose_mg": 100, "note": "Dose must be calculated based on hemoglobin deficit. Do not exceed maximum daily limits based on weight."}}]', 'Contraindicated in acute renal failure. Caution should be exercised when giving Iron Dextran to patients with chronic renal impairment, as altered iron utilization may occur.', '- **Test Dose:** Administer 0.5 mL slowly over at least 30 seconds (IV) or via deep IM injection. Wait 1 hour before administering the remainder of the therapeutic dose.
- **Intravenous Administration:** May be given undiluted at a rate not exceeding 50 mg (1 mL) per minute. Alternatively, dilute the calculated total dose in 250-1000 mL of 0.9% Sodium Chloride and infuse over 1-6 hours. Infuse the first 25 mL slowly and observe for allergic reactions.
- **Intramuscular Administration:** Inject deeply into the upper outer quadrant of the buttock using the Z-track technique to prevent subcutaneous leakage and permanent brown skin staining. Do not inject into the arm or other exposed areas.', '- **Acute:** Hypotension, shock, lethargy, tachycardia, nausea, vomiting, diarrhea, metabolic acidosis.
