- **Ultimate Clinical Outcome:** Symptoms are generally self-limiting and resolve with supportive care. No life-threatening outcomes are expected from an overdose of this inactivated vaccine.', '- **Management:** Provide symptomatic treatment. Use cold compresses for local injection site reactions. Administer oral antipyretics/analgesics (e.g., acetaminophen) for fever and pain.', '- Store in a refrigerator between 2°C and 8°C (36°F to 46°F).
- Do not freeze. Discard if the vaccine has been frozen.
- Protect from light.', '- This vaccine helps protect against typhoid fever, but it is not 100% effective. You must still be careful about what you eat and drink while traveling (e.g., drink bottled water, avoid raw vegetables and ice).
