- The vaccine should be given at least 2 weeks before you travel to ensure your body has time to build immunity.
- If you continue to travel to high-risk areas, you will need a booster shot every 2 to 3 years.', '("Typhoid-Paratyphoid Vaccines"[Mesh] OR "typhoid polysaccharide vaccine"[tiab] OR "Vi capsular polysaccharide vaccine"[tiab])');
- Do not cover topical applications with occlusive dressings, as this increases systemic absorption and local tissue irritation.
