**Rare but Serious:**
- Severe allergic reactions (rash, itching/swelling of the face/tongue/throat, severe dizziness, trouble breathing)', 'Data not available', '**Risk Summary:** FDA has not classified this combination into a specified pregnancy category. However, systemic absorption of these topical ingredients is minimal to non-existent. It is generally considered safe for use during pregnancy when applied as directed.', 'Considered safe for use during lactation. If applied to the breast area, wash thoroughly before nursing to prevent accidental ingestion by the infant.', '{"trimester_1": "Safe", "trimester_2": "Safe", "trimester_3": "Safe"}', 'This combination provides cooling itch relief, physical barrier protection, and moisture retention for irritated skin.', '["Calamine (a mixture of zinc oxide and a small amount of ferric oxide) acts as an antipruritic. As its aqueous base evaporates, it draws heat away from the skin, producing a cooling effect that depresses local sensory nerves to relieve itching.", "Zinc Oxide acts as a mild astringent and physical barrier. It shields the epidermis from external irritants, contracts skin tissues, and reduces minor exudation (weeping) from lesions.", "Glycerin acts as a humectant. It draws atmospheric moisture into the stratum corneum, counteracting the drying effects of zinc and calamine, maintaining skin hydration, and softening rough, irritated areas."]', '**Moderate:**
- **No known significant drug interactions:** Because systemic absorption is negligible, it does not interact with systemic medications. Avoid applying other topical medications simultaneously to the same area, as the barrier effect of zinc oxide may prevent their absorption.', '**Minor Skin Irritations:**
