**Clinical Considerations:**
If pregnancy occurs following the administration of this drug, the patient should be monitored closely, as Ovarian Hyperstimulation Syndrome (OHSS) can be more severe and protracted if pregnancy is achieved.', '**Pregnancy:**
Choriogonadotropin alfa is contraindicated during pregnancy. Animal studies have demonstrated intrauterine death and impaired parturition when administered during pregnancy. The drug is intended solely for the induction of ovulation and has no therapeutic role once pregnancy is established.

**Lactation:**
It is not known whether choriogonadotropin alfa is excreted in human milk. Because many drugs are excreted in human milk, caution should be exercised if administered to a nursing woman. The developmental and health benefits of breastfeeding should be considered along with the mother’s clinical need for therapy and any potential adverse effects on the breastfed child.', '{"trimester_1": "Contraindicated", "trimester_2": "Contraindicated", "trimester_3": "Contraindicated"}', 'Choriogonadotropin alfa is a recombinant human chorionic gonadotropin that mimics the action of luteinizing hormone (LH) to trigger final follicular maturation and ovulation.', '["Choriogonadotropin alfa binds to the luteinizing hormone/chorionic gonadotropin (LH/CG) transmembrane receptors on the ovarian theca and granulosa cells.", "Receptor activation initiates an intracellular cascade mediated by cyclic AMP (cAMP).", "This cascade stimulates late follicular maturation, resumption of oocyte meiosis, and initiates the rupture of the pre-ovulatory ovarian follicle (ovulation).", "Following ovulation, it promotes the development and maintenance of the corpus luteum, which produces progesterone to support early pregnancy."]', '**Immunological Pregnancy Tests:**
- **Clinical Result:** Administration of choriogonadotropin alfa may interfere with the immunological determination of serum or urinary human chorionic gonadotropin (hCG) for up to 10 days.
- **Management:** Advise patients that pregnancy tests may yield false-positive results during this 10-day window. Confirm pregnancy status using quantitative serum hCG trends or ultrasound.', '- **Induction of Ovulation & Pregnancy / Assisted Reproductive Technology (ART):**
  - Administer 250 mcg subcutaneously (SC) as a single dose one day following the last dose of the follicle-stimulating agent.
  - Use only after adequate follicular development has been determined via serum estradiol and transvaginal ultrasound.
