  - *Timing:* Initiate during the mid-to-late follicular phase (typically on day 6 of FSH administration, which usually starts on day 2 or 3 of the cycle).
  - *Duration:* Continue daily treatment until the day of human chorionic gonadotropin (hCG) administration. When ultrasound assessment shows sufficient follicles of adequate size, administer hCG to induce final maturation.', '- **Pediatric Population:**
  - Safety and efficacy have not been established. Ganirelix is not indicated for use in children.', '[]', '- **Mild Renal Impairment:** Use with caution.
