**Macular Edema:** Macular edema, including cystoid macular edema, has been reported. Use with caution in aphakic patients, pseudophakic patients with a torn posterior lens capsule, or patients with known risk factors for macular edema.
**Contact Lenses:** Contains preservatives that may be absorbed by soft contact lenses. Remove lenses prior to instillation and wait 15 minutes before reinserting.', '- **Elevated Intraocular Pressure:** Indicated for the reduction of elevated intraocular pressure (IOP) in patients with open-angle glaucoma or ocular hypertension.', '**Hypersensitivity:** Contraindicated in patients with known hypersensitivity to tafluprost or any of its excipients. Rationale: Can cause severe local allergic reactions, including conjunctival hyperemia and swelling.', '- **Common (>10%):** Conjunctival hyperemia.
- **Less Common (1-10%):** Ocular stinging, ocular pruritus, allergic conjunctivitis, cataract, growth of eyelashes, blurred vision, dry eye, ocular pain.
