Excretion in breast milk is unknown. If used, avoid application to the chest/breast area to prevent accidental ingestion by the infant.', '{"trimester_1": "Not established", "trimester_2": "Not established", "trimester_3": "Not established"}', 'Calcipotriol is a synthetic vitamin D3 analog that binds to vitamin D receptors on epidermal cells, inhibiting keratinocyte proliferation and promoting their normal differentiation.', '["Calcipotriol penetrates the stratum corneum and binds to the intracellular vitamin D receptor (VDR) in epidermal keratinocytes.", "The calcipotriol-VDR complex translocates to the nucleus and binds to specific DNA response elements.", "This interaction modulates the transcription of genes involved in epidermal proliferation and differentiation.", "The net result is a suppression of the abnormally rapid proliferation of keratinocytes and an induction of normal cellular differentiation, reducing psoriatic plaque formation."]', '**Topical Salicylic Acid:**
*Clinical Result:* Salicylic acid can rapidly inactivate calcipotriol due to its acidic nature.
*Management:* Do not apply calcipotriol and topical salicylic acid at the same time or on the same skin area. If both are needed, apply them at different times of the day.

**Systemic Calcium or Vitamin D Supplements:**
*Clinical Result:* Increased risk of hypercalcemia.
*Management:* Monitor serum calcium levels closely if concurrent use is necessary.', '**Plaque Psoriasis:**
