It is not known whether topical ophthalmic or otic administration results in sufficient systemic absorption to produce detectable quantities in breast milk. Use with caution in nursing mothers.', '{"trimester_1": "Not established", "trimester_2": "Not established", "trimester_3": "Not established"}', 'This combination provides dual bactericidal action against Gram-positive and Gram-negative organisms along with the anti-inflammatory effect of a corticosteroid.', '["Neomycin actively transports into the bacterial cell and binds irreversibly to the 30S ribosomal subunit, causing misreading of mRNA and inhibiting protein synthesis.", "Polymyxin B binds to the lipopolysaccharide of the Gram-negative bacterial outer membrane, altering membrane permeability and causing leakage of intracellular contents.", "Hydrocortisone diffuses into local cells and binds to glucocorticoid receptors, inhibiting phospholipase A2.", "This suppresses the release of arachidonic acid, reducing the synthesis of prostaglandins and leukotrienes, thereby decreasing local inflammation, edema, and pruritus."]', '- **Systemic Aminoglycosides/Polymyxins:** Additive toxicity (neurotoxic, ototoxic, or nephrotoxic) if significant systemic absorption occurs. *Management:* Avoid concurrent use if possible.
- **Neuromuscular Blocking Agents:** Increased neuromuscular blockade and possibly respiratory depression if significant amounts of neomycin are absorbed. *Management:* Monitor closely if concurrent use is necessary.', '- **Ocular Inflammation with Suspected/Confirmed Bacterial Infection:**
  - *Ophthalmic Drops:* Instill 1 to 2 drops into the conjunctival sac(s) every 3 to 4 hours, or more frequently as indicated by the severity of the infection.
- **Otitis Externa:**
  - *Otic Drops:* Instill 4 drops into the affected ear 3 to 4 times daily. 
  - *Alternative:* Insert a cotton wick into the canal and saturate the wick with the solution. Add solution every 4 hours to keep the wick moist. Replace the wick at least once daily.
  - *Duration:* Limit treatment to 10 days.', '- **Otitis Externa:**
  - *Children 2 to 16 years:* Instill 3 drops into the affected ear 3 to 4 times daily. 
  - *Alternative:* Insert a cotton wick into the canal and saturate the wick with the solution. Add solution every 4 hours to keep the wick moist. Replace the wick at least once daily.
  - *Duration:* Limit treatment to 10 days.', '[{"target_group": "Children (2 to 16 years)", "min_age_months": 24, "max_age_months": 192, "dosing_type": "fixed_dose", "parameters": {"fixed_dose_mg": 0, "frequency_hours": 6, "note": "Instill 3 drops into the affected ear 3 to 4 times daily. Maximum duration of 10 days."}}]', 'No dosage adjustment is required for topical ophthalmic or otic use. However, caution should be exercised if significant systemic absorption is suspected in patients with severe renal impairment.', '- **Ophthalmic:** Wash hands before use. Tilt head back, pull down the lower eyelid, and instill drops into the conjunctival sac. Close the eye and apply gentle pressure to the inner corner for 1-2 minutes to minimize systemic absorption. Do not touch the dropper tip to any surface.
- **Otic:** Shake well before use. Lie on your side or tilt the affected ear upward. Instill drops and remain in this position for 5 minutes to allow the medication to penetrate the ear canal. Do not touch the dropper tip to the ear.', '- **Acute Overdose:** Topical overdose is unlikely to cause acute systemic toxicity. Accidental ingestion may cause gastrointestinal upset.
- **Chronic Overdose:** Prolonged ophthalmic use can cause glaucoma, optic nerve damage, and cataracts. Prolonged otic use (especially with a perforated eardrum) can cause irreversible ototoxicity and neomycin sensitization.', '- **Management:** Discontinue the medication immediately. Monitor intraocular pressure if ophthalmic overdose is suspected. Evaluate hearing if otic overdose/toxicity is suspected. Treat symptomatically.', 'Store at controlled room temperature (15°C to 25°C). Protect from light. Keep the bottle tightly closed. Do not freeze.', '- Shake the bottle well before each use.
- For ear drops: Lie on your side with the affected ear facing up, instill the drops, and stay in that position for 5 minutes to let the medicine reach the infection.
