- **Standard Dose:** 45 mg twice daily.', 'Safety and efficacy not established in pediatric patients.', '[]', 'Caution should be exercised when giving Gefapixant to patients with severe renal impairment (eGFR <30 mL/min/1.73 m²), as renal excretion is the major route of elimination and systemic exposure may significantly increase. Dose adjustment may be required.', 'Administer orally twice daily. May be taken with or without food. Swallow the tablet whole.', '- **Moderate:** Exacerbation of taste disturbances (severe dysgeusia or ageusia), dry mouth, gastrointestinal discomfort.
