**External Use Only:** Advise patients that the medication is for topical external use only and should not be ingested or applied to mucosal surfaces.', '- Treatment of plaque psoriasis in adults.', '**Hypersensitivity:** Contraindicated in patients with a known hypersensitivity to tapinarof or any of the excipients in the formulation.
*Rationale:* Risk of severe allergic contact dermatitis or hypersensitivity reactions.', '- **Common (>10%):** Folliculitis (20%), nasopharyngitis (including nasal congestion, pharyngitis, viral respiratory tract infection, rhinorrhea, sinus congestion) (11%).
- **Frequent (1-10%):** Contact dermatitis (including hand dermatitis and rash) (7%), headache (including migraine and tension headache) (4%), pruritus (including application site, generalized, and genital pruritus) (3%), influenza (including influenza-like illness) (2%).', 'C', '**Pregnancy Risk:**
