It is not known whether the components are excreted in human milk following topical application. Caution should be exercised when administered to a nursing woman. Ensure the medication is not applied to the breast area prior to feeding.', '{"trimester_1": "Not established", "trimester_2": "Not established", "trimester_3": "Not established"}', 'This combination provides broad-spectrum antibacterial action via neomycin and polymyxin B, and local anesthesia via pramoxine.', '["Neomycin binds to the 30S ribosomal subunit of susceptible bacteria, inhibiting protein synthesis and causing cell death.", "Polymyxin B binds to the lipopolysaccharide of the Gram-negative bacterial cell membrane, altering its permeability and causing leakage of intracellular contents.", "Pramoxine acts as a local anesthetic by decreasing the permeability of neuronal membranes to sodium ions, blocking the initiation and conduction of nerve impulses, thereby relieving pain."]', '- **Systemic Aminoglycosides:** Additive nephrotoxicity and ototoxicity may occur if significant systemic absorption of topical neomycin occurs concurrently with systemic aminoglycoside therapy.
- **Neuromuscular Blocking Agents:** Neomycin has neuromuscular blocking activity; systemic absorption could theoretically potentiate these agents.', '### Topical
