  - Safety and efficacy have not been fully established. Use with extreme caution due to the risk of severe systemic effects (apnea, bradycardia). If used, instill 1 drop into the affected eye(s) twice daily under strict medical supervision.', '[]', 'Caution should be exercised when giving this combination to patients with renal impairment, as it has not been formally studied in this population.', 'For ophthalmic use only. Wash hands before use. Do not touch the dropper tip to the eye or any surface. After instilling the drop, perform nasolacrimal occlusion (press the inner corner of the eye) for 1 to 2 minutes to minimize systemic absorption of timolol and brimonidine. If using other ophthalmic medications, wait at least 5 minutes between applications.', '- **Ophthalmic Overdose:** Severe ocular irritation, hyperemia.
- **Systemic Overdose:** Bradycardia, hypotension, bronchospasm, acute cardiac failure, apnea, hypothermia, severe CNS depression, somnolence, and coma.', '- **Management:** Flush eyes with water or normal saline. For systemic absorption/ingestion, provide immediate supportive care. Treat bradycardia with IV atropine (or isoproterenol if refractory). Treat hypotension with IV fluids and vasopressors. Treat bronchospasm with a beta-2 agonist (e.g., albuterol) or IV aminophylline. Maintain a patent airway.', 'Store at room temperature (15°C to 25°C). Protect from light. Keep the bottle tightly closed.', 'To prevent the medicine from entering your bloodstream and causing heart or breathing problems, press your finger against the inner corner of your eye for 1 to 2 minutes after putting in the drop. Tell your doctor if you have asthma or heart problems before using this medication. Remove contact lenses before use and wait 15 minutes before reinserting them.', '((("Brimonidine Tartrate"[mh] OR "Brimonidine Tartrate"[tiab]) AND ("Timolol"[mh] OR "Timolol"[tiab] OR "Timolol Maleate"[tiab])) AND ("ophthalmic"[tiab] OR "ocular"[tiab] OR "eye"[tiab]))');
**Tuberculosis (TB):** Evaluate for TB prior to initiation. Do not administer to patients with active TB. Initiate treatment for latent TB prior to starting risankizumab. Monitor for signs and symptoms of active TB during treatment.
**Immunizations:** Complete all age-appropriate immunizations before initiating therapy. Avoid the use of live vaccines during treatment.', '- **Plaque Psoriasis:** Indicated for the treatment of moderate-to-severe plaque psoriasis in adults who are candidates for systemic therapy or phototherapy.', '- **Hypersensitivity:** Contraindicated in patients with a history of serious hypersensitivity reactions to risankizumab or any of its excipients. Rationale: Risk of anaphylaxis or severe allergic reactions.', '**>10%**
