  - Take 1 tablet orally every 4 hours as needed while symptoms persist.
  - **Maximum Dose:** Do not exceed 6 tablets in a 24-hour period.', '[{"target_group": "Neonates and Infants", "min_age_months": 0, "max_age_months": 143, "dosing_type": "weight_based", "parameters": {"mg_per_kg_per_day_min": 0, "mg_per_kg_per_day_max": 0, "divided_doses_per_day": [0], "note": "Safety and efficacy not established. Avoid use in this age group."}}, {"target_group": "Adolescents", "min_age_months": 144, "max_age_months": 216, "dosing_type": "fixed_dose", "parameters": {"fixed_dose_mg": 200, "frequency_hours": 4, "note": "Dose based on standard tablet formulation. 1 tablet every 4 hours. Max 6 tablets/day."}}]', 'Caution should be exercised when giving this combination to patients with renal impairment. Ibuprofen can cause a dose-dependent reduction in prostaglandin formation and precipitate overt renal decompensation. Avoid use in patients with severe renal impairment (CrCl < 30 mL/min).', '- Administer orally with a full glass of water.
