*Note:* Safety and efficacy in children under 3 years of age have not been established.', '[]', 'No dosage adjustment is required. Systemic absorption is minimal.', '- For topical ophthalmic use only.
- Wash hands before use.
- Tilt head back, pull down the lower eyelid to form a pouch, and instill the drop.
- Do not touch the dropper tip to the eye, eyelid, or any other surface to avoid contamination.
- If using other eye drops, wait at least 5 minutes between applications.
- Remove contact lenses prior to administration and wait at least 10 minutes before reinserting.', 'Overdose via the ocular route is highly unlikely to cause systemic toxicity. Accidental oral ingestion may cause mild CNS depression, somnolence, and cardiac arrhythmias in extreme cases.', '**Management Strategy:**
- For topical ocular overdose, flush the eyes with sterile water or normal saline.
- For accidental oral ingestion, treatment is symptomatic and supportive. Monitor vital signs and observe for excessive sedation.', 'Store at 4°C to 25°C (39°F to 77°F). Keep the bottle tightly closed when not in use.', '- Do not use this medication to treat irritation caused by wearing contact lenses.
- If your eyes are red, do not wear contact lenses.
