**<1% (Rare but Serious)**
- Hypersensitivity reactions (anaphylaxis, skin rash, urticaria)
- Respiratory symptoms (tachypnea, dyspnea)
- Circulatory effects (hypertension, hypotension)
- Fat overload syndrome (hyperlipidemia, fever, hepatosplenomegaly, coagulopathy)
- Thrombosis or phlebitis at the infusion site
- Hemolysis, reticulocytosis
- Neurological reactions (headache, flushing, dizziness)', 'C', '**Pregnancy Exposure Risk**
