It is unknown if topical salicylic acid is excreted in breast milk. It is generally considered safe, but avoid application to the chest area to prevent accidental ingestion by the nursing infant.', '{"trimester_1": "Safe", "trimester_2": "Safe", "trimester_3": "Safe"}', 'Salicylic acid is a keratolytic agent that promotes the shedding of the stratum corneum and unclogs pores.', '["Topically applied salicylic acid penetrates the lipid barrier of the stratum corneum.", "It reduces intercellular cohesion between corneocytes by dissolving the intercellular cement.", "This increases endogenous hydration, causing the horny layer of the skin to swell, soften, and desquamate.", "The resulting exfoliation unclogs pores, exerting a mild comedolytic and anti-inflammatory effect."]', '- **Other Topical Acne Preparations (e.g., Benzoyl Peroxide, Retinoids):** (Moderate) Increased risk of severe skin dryness, peeling, and irritation. Management: Use cautiously; consider alternating application times (e.g., one in the morning, one at night).', '- **Acne / Scaling Conditions:** Apply a thin layer to the affected area 1 to 3 times daily. If excessive dryness or peeling occurs, reduce application to once daily or every other day.', '- **Children > 2 years:** Apply a thin layer to the affected area 1 to 3 times daily. Reduce frequency if dryness occurs.
