**Arrhythmias with Rapid Injection:** Potentially life-threatening arrhythmias have been reported in patients who received rapid (less than 60 seconds) intravenous bolus injections of cefotaxime through a central venous catheter. Administer slowly over 3 to 5 minutes.
**Granulocytopenia:** Granulocytopenia and, more rarely, agranulocytosis may develop during treatment, particularly if given over long periods. Monitor blood counts if treatment lasts longer than 10 days.', '- **Lower Respiratory Tract Infections:** Treatment of pneumonia, acute/chronic bronchitis, infected bronchiectasis, and lung abscess.
