- Systemic toxicity (only with extensive coverage, prolonged use, or highly toxic active ingredients)', 'Data not available', '**Risk Summary:** Varies widely by individual drug. Always evaluate specific drug monographs before use in pregnancy. Generally, inert emollients and protectants are safe, while agents with systemic absorption risks (e.g., topical retinoids, high-dose salicylic acid) should be avoided or minimized.', 'Varies by agent. Generally, avoid applying topical medications directly to the breast or nipple area prior to nursing to prevent accidental ingestion by the infant.', '{"trimester_1": "Not established", "trimester_2": "Not established", "trimester_3": "Not established"}', 'Topical agents exert their effects locally on the skin through various mechanisms depending on their specific class.', '["**Keratolytics (e.g., salicylic acid, urea):** Dissolve intercellular cement to desquamate the stratum corneum and soften hyperkeratotic skin.", "**Anti-infectives:** Alter microbial cell wall permeability or inhibit microbial protein synthesis locally at the site of infection.", "**Protectants/Emollients (e.g., zinc oxide, petrolatum):** Provide a physical, hydrophobic barrier to moisture and irritants, trapping water in the skin to restore hydration.", "**Astringents (e.g., calamine, witch hazel):** Coagulate proteins and contract skin tissues to dry out weeping or oozing lesions."]', '**Moderate:**
